00:03:00.106 --> 00:03:01.034
- [Interviewer] How do you feel about

00:03:01.034 --> 00:03:02.458
things that happened to you in the past?

00:03:02.458 --> 00:03:04.267
For example, you going to jail,

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:05.938
you getting fired from
a couple of stations.

00:03:05.938 --> 00:03:07.618
You think that might have been

00:03:07.618 --> 00:03:10.840
the stuff you were putting out
there that came back to you?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.673
- Well--

00:03:11.673 --> 00:03:12.506
- You were making some dumb decisions--

00:03:12.506 --> 00:03:13.339
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:13.339 --> 00:03:16.597
When I was getting locked
up, I didn't know no better.

00:03:16.597 --> 00:03:18.435
I think when you know
better, you do better.

00:03:18.435 --> 00:03:20.484
That's why I say, when I
wanted to change my life,

00:03:20.484 --> 00:03:22.251
I changed my lifestyle.

00:03:22.251 --> 00:03:24.787
So, I started knowing better,
so I started doing better.

00:03:24.787 --> 00:03:26.060
As far as me getting fired,

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.892
that's just the way things are sometimes.

00:03:28.892 --> 00:03:30.660
- How'd you come up in radio?
How'd you start with radio?

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.569
- I started off as an intern in 1998

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:33.669
when I was 18 years old.

00:03:33.669 --> 00:03:34.844
I'm 32 now.

00:03:34.844 --> 00:03:35.988
I've been doing radio for--

00:03:35.988 --> 00:03:37.444
this'll be my 15th year in radio.

00:03:37.444 --> 00:03:39.570
I started off as an intern when I was 18.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.436
So, I've worked in every aspect of radio.

00:03:42.436 --> 00:03:45.452
I've worked in the promotions department.

00:03:45.452 --> 00:03:46.520
I worked in programming.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.566
I was an intern for a year and a half.

00:03:49.566 --> 00:03:51.902
This is the 7th radio
station I've worked at.

00:03:51.902 --> 00:03:53.198
I've been fired four times.

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:54.175
- Okay.

00:03:54.175 --> 00:03:55.830
- So it's like--

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.574
That's why, when I saw William,

00:03:57.574 --> 00:03:59.807
I go, "William came back
out there to perform".

00:03:59.807 --> 00:04:01.981
For everybody who wasn't at the show,

00:04:01.981 --> 00:04:03.961
William was a rapper who got booed,

00:04:03.961 --> 00:04:06.657
but he forced them to
let him perform again.

00:04:06.657 --> 00:04:08.153
I just like the determination.

00:04:08.153 --> 00:04:09.278
- Right.

00:04:09.278 --> 00:04:11.001
- The never say "quit" attitude

00:04:11.001 --> 00:04:13.470
'cause that's what you have to have.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.311
Like I said, I've been fired four times,

00:04:14.311 --> 00:04:15.575
I could have quit a long time ago,

00:04:15.575 --> 00:04:16.751
but I don't have no backup plan.

00:04:16.751 --> 00:04:19.390
I didn't go to college,
I don't have a degree.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.349
I don't have anything
else to do, but radio.

00:04:22.349 --> 00:04:23.188
I used to want to rap,

00:04:23.188 --> 00:04:25.868
until I realized that rap
was just a pipe dream.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:30.394
It's so many things that
you go through in this game.

00:04:30.394 --> 00:04:32.274
So many ebbs and flows,
so many ups and downs,

00:04:32.274 --> 00:04:35.578
but it's the people that
truly keep going that make it.

00:04:35.578 --> 00:04:37.042
- What's your vision board look like?

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:38.082
So, you have--

00:04:38.082 --> 00:04:39.010
I'm sorry go ahead,

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.043
tell me what your vision board looks like

00:04:40.043 --> 00:04:42.532
and can you share some of
the things that are on there?

00:04:42.532 --> 00:04:44.083
- I used to have a
traditional vision board,

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.678
where you would take things that you want

00:04:47.678 --> 00:04:49.811
and put them up on poster board

00:04:49.811 --> 00:04:50.644
and that's cool.

00:04:50.644 --> 00:04:51.923
I did that when I did The Secret,

00:04:51.923 --> 00:04:54.844
but, to me, the best vision
boards are when you write down

00:04:54.844 --> 00:04:56.092
your long-term and short-term goals.

00:04:56.092 --> 00:04:57.588
Write down everything that
you want to accomplish

00:04:57.588 --> 00:05:01.497
and keep those things in your mind because

00:05:01.497 --> 00:05:03.711
your mind is what makes
them manifest into reality.

00:05:03.711 --> 00:05:05.271
Your thoughts really do become things.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:08.376
I don't have a college
degree, or anything like that.

00:05:08.376 --> 00:05:10.760
All I have is, back in 1998,

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.315
I said, "I want to be a Super Jock".

00:05:13.315 --> 00:05:15.256
I said, "I want to be one of
the biggest radio personalities

00:05:15.256 --> 00:05:16.089
on the planet".

00:05:16.089 --> 00:05:20.256
I said, "I want to be in that
Wendy Williams, Tom Joyner,

00:05:21.523 --> 00:05:26.518
Doug Banks, Howard Stern,
Bill O'Reilly, Rush Limbaugh.

00:05:26.518 --> 00:05:28.037
I want to be in that number".

00:05:28.037 --> 00:05:28.958
When they think of Charlamagne,

00:05:28.958 --> 00:05:30.478
I want them to think of me like that.

00:05:30.478 --> 00:05:31.777
I want to be my generation's that.

00:05:31.777 --> 00:05:34.222
Because all of those guys,

00:05:34.222 --> 00:05:36.505
it's the natural cause of thing
that power eventually fades

00:05:36.505 --> 00:05:37.338
and weakens.

00:05:37.338 --> 00:05:39.407
All of them, it's just
like the NBA or music.

00:05:39.407 --> 00:05:42.458
It was the Magic Johnson, Larry Bird era.

00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:43.693
Then it was the Michael Jordan era,

00:05:43.693 --> 00:05:44.673
now it's the LeBron James era.

00:05:44.673 --> 00:05:46.522
That's just the way things are in the game

00:05:46.522 --> 00:05:48.934
and I knew that, eventually,
it would be my time

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.757
if I wanted that.

00:05:50.757 --> 00:05:51.693
So, I claimed it.

00:05:51.693 --> 00:05:55.283
So, my vision board is a
really, just a notebook,

00:05:55.283 --> 00:05:57.637
with everything that I want in my life.

00:05:57.637 --> 00:05:59.059
Live your truth, man.

00:05:59.059 --> 00:06:00.382
Live your truth.

00:06:00.382 --> 00:06:01.862
When you live your truth,

00:06:01.862 --> 00:06:03.501
nobody can use your truth against you

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:07.489
and the world opens up
for an honest person.

00:06:07.489 --> 00:06:09.430
You get back what you put out,

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:13.263
so if you're always
consistently being honest,

00:06:14.693 --> 00:06:17.585
you'll get honest things
that'll come back to you.

00:06:17.585 --> 00:06:19.189
With honesty comes positivity.

00:06:19.189 --> 00:06:21.285
So, when you give out positive energy,

00:06:21.285 --> 00:06:22.541
you get back positive energy.

00:06:22.541 --> 00:06:24.230
You get back positive things.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.541
So, that's why I always tell people,

00:06:25.541 --> 00:06:28.349
"Let your foundation be
a foundation of honesty".

00:06:28.349 --> 00:06:30.786
Just always live your truth.

00:06:30.786 --> 00:06:31.934
Yeah, and even when you look on Instagram,

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.358
look at someone like Cardi B,

00:06:33.358 --> 00:06:35.793
who is very famous on Instagram.

00:06:35.793 --> 00:06:39.300
I feel like she was just honing a craft.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.940
That's why, when you see
her in front of the camera,

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.596
on Love &amp; Hip Hop, she pops.

00:06:43.596 --> 00:06:44.541
- Right.

00:06:44.541 --> 00:06:45.582
- She already got a natural personality,

00:06:45.582 --> 00:06:46.660
but she knows how to operate
in front of that camera.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:47.708
- Right.

00:06:47.708 --> 00:06:50.004
- So, I think it helps,

00:06:50.004 --> 00:06:51.628
I just don't think it
should be your only hustle.

00:06:51.628 --> 00:06:52.540
- It can't be, right.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.881
- I think it should be something
to cultivate your craft

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:57.523
and get you to a point,

00:06:57.523 --> 00:06:59.156
but then there's always another level.

00:06:59.156 --> 00:07:01.198
I look at a rapper, like Young M.A.

00:07:01.198 --> 00:07:02.089
- Yeah

00:07:02.089 --> 00:07:03.674
She got ten million views on YouTube.

00:07:03.674 --> 00:07:05.426
Everybody loves her, but now,

00:07:05.426 --> 00:07:07.433
you got to get to that next level.

00:07:07.433 --> 00:07:09.936
You got to get a record
deal, if you want one.

00:07:09.936 --> 00:07:11.120
You don't really need
one of those nowadays,

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.824
but if you want one, you
get a record deal, or--

00:07:12.824 --> 00:07:14.682
You just got to figure out
how to really be a star.

00:07:14.682 --> 00:07:15.760
You got to look at the goals.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.256
You want to be on the VMAs,

00:07:17.256 --> 00:07:20.840
you want to perform at the BET
awards, you want to win Grammys.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.216
But the reason I made it is because

00:07:22.216 --> 00:07:24.069
I knew exactly what I wanted to do.

00:07:24.069 --> 00:07:25.848
See, that's the thing I see
with a lot of people nowadays.

00:07:25.848 --> 00:07:26.681
They be confused.

00:07:26.681 --> 00:07:31.005
They don't really have a
clear-cut, concise goal in mind.

00:07:31.005 --> 00:07:32.922
They don't have that one thing that

00:07:32.922 --> 00:07:34.262
they feel that they're good at,

00:07:34.262 --> 00:07:35.820
so they don't try to master it.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:36.653
I'm reading a book right now called

00:07:36.653 --> 00:07:37.861
The Mastery by Robert Greene.

00:07:37.861 --> 00:07:40.828
It's basically taking that
whole 10,000 hour theory.

00:07:40.828 --> 00:07:42.418
You're not a master at something until

00:07:42.418 --> 00:07:44.004
you've put in 10,000 hours.

00:07:44.004 --> 00:07:44.837
- You've practiced for 10,000 hours.

00:07:44.837 --> 00:07:47.228
- Yeah, so you got to find that one thing

00:07:47.228 --> 00:07:48.612
to put in that time with

00:07:48.612 --> 00:07:50.196
and everything else will sprout from it.

00:07:50.196 --> 00:07:52.324
Radio was my thing and then I'm--

00:07:52.324 --> 00:07:53.860
- So I was going to say,
you always knew then radio?

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:54.693
- Always.

00:07:54.693 --> 00:07:56.532
People move on.

00:07:56.532 --> 00:07:57.908
They go.

00:07:57.908 --> 00:08:01.898
50 actually put out some great
records earlier this year.

00:08:01.898 --> 00:08:03.343
The joint he had with Kendrick Lamar,

00:08:03.343 --> 00:08:04.548
then he had another record.

00:08:04.548 --> 00:08:06.540
The joint with Too Short,
I thought was dope,

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.423
but when people are off
you, they are off you.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:13.103
He got his pocket of fans
that'll still support him,

00:08:13.103 --> 00:08:14.639
but you'll never see 50 Cent selling

00:08:14.639 --> 00:08:15.967
