00:08:15.967 --> 00:08:18.751
Hell, you'll never 50 Cent
selling a million records again.

00:08:18.751 --> 00:08:21.769
Not on one album, he
might do it as a single

00:08:21.769 --> 00:08:25.489
and that's not a diss
to him, that's just--

00:08:25.489 --> 00:08:26.470
- [Interviewer] That's the way hip-hop is.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:29.604
- That's the way hip-hop
is, nobody cares no more.

00:08:29.604 --> 00:08:32.127
A thug changes, love changes

00:08:32.127 --> 00:08:33.261
and best friends become strangers.

00:08:33.261 --> 00:08:35.381
It happens all the time,
it happens in cycles.

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:37.380
Everybody can't be Jay-Z.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:41.318
The reason Jay-Z is Jay-Z,
but Jay-Z has been consistent.

00:08:41.318 --> 00:08:44.220
Jay-Z dropped an album
every year since 1996.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.955
My father was into construction,
so I used to help him out,

00:08:48.955 --> 00:08:51.787
as far as building houses
and stuff like that,

00:08:51.787 --> 00:08:53.851
but I didn't really start working until

00:08:53.851 --> 00:08:55.627
I got out of jail for the first time.

00:08:55.627 --> 00:08:57.072
When I got out of jail for the first time,

00:08:57.072 --> 00:08:59.492
I did a year in jail
for assault and battery

00:08:59.492 --> 00:09:00.325
with intent to kill

00:09:00.325 --> 00:09:01.158
and the only reason I did a year,

00:09:01.158 --> 00:09:02.467
'cause my father was
trying to teach me a lesson

00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:03.971
'cause I was such a bad kid.

00:09:03.971 --> 00:09:05.267
So, he was trying to teach me a lesson,

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:07.491
so instead of posting my
bail, he let me sit in jail

00:09:07.491 --> 00:09:11.658
and I'm like, I don't know,
16, 17 at the time in '97.

00:09:12.866 --> 00:09:14.528
'96, '97? Yeah.

00:09:14.528 --> 00:09:18.540
So, when I got out of jail
